==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|sitia}}, from {{inh|sv|non|sitja}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*sitjaną}}, from {{inh|sv|ine-pro|*sed-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/²sɪta/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-sitta.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|sv|²ɪta}}

===Verb===
{{sv-verb-irr|sitter|satt|suttit|sitt}}

# to [[sit]] {{gloss|be in a position with the upper body upright and the legs resting}}
#: {{ux|sv|Jag '''sitter''' på stolen|I'm '''sitting''' on the chair}}
#: {{ux|sv|Hon [[böra|bör]] '''sitta''' i [[båt]]en.|She should be '''sitting''' in the boat.}}
# to [[sit]] (more generally, similar to English)
#: {{ux|sv|Det '''sitter''' en fluga på taket|There's a fly '''sitting''' on the ceiling}}
#: {{ux|sv|Det '''sitter''' en spik i väggen|There is a nail in the wall ("There is a nail sitting in the wall" – idiomatic in Swedish)}}
# {{lb|sv|politics}} to sit {{gloss|be a member of a committee or a deliberative body}}

====Usage notes====
* The class 3 conjugation was formed by analogy with verbs like {{m|sv|finna}} or {{m|sv|dricka}}, replacing the earlier inherited class 5 conjugation, which mostly disappeared in the latter half of the 18th century.

